 Topology
 --------
 RTL8197F/RTL8197FH-VG physical P0/RGMII <-> RTL8367D CPU7/EXT1.
 Linux DSA owns the 8-byte rtl8_4 tag and bridge/VLAN/FDB/STP state.
 
-V38 platform extensions
------------------------
-1. P0/RGMII is programmed during NIC probe, before the external DSA switch.
-2. RTL8197FH/VG PITCR and EXTPCR0 use the BSP 8-byte IPG fields.
-3. The RTL8197F interrupt controller supports both 32-input banks (64 HWIRQs).
-4. UART0/1/2 use BSP HWIRQs 9/38/39; UART1/2 remain board-disabled by default.
-5. Native USB2 host glue performs clock/mode/PHY setup and instantiates generic
-   EHCI/OHCI children. The RD05 board keeps USB disabled unless hardware routing
-   is confirmed.
-6. RTL8367 family matching includes legacy IDs 0x0276, 0x0597, family ID 0x6367
-   and RTL8367D/RB-VC ID 0x6642 with the family-D register model.
-7. The persistent timing file is PROFILE_VERSION=38. Older experimental profiles
-   are backed up as /etc/rd05-rgmii.conf.pre-v38 and migrated to the SDK baseline.
+Boot-proven platform state
+--------------------------
+- UART0/ttyS0 is 0x18147000 at 115200 8N1 and uses polling on RD05.
+- RTL8197F uses the stable first 32-input interrupt bank on RD05.
+- P0/RGMII programming is deferred to ndo_open.
+- SPI-NOR WEL calibration is lazy and rootfs_data-only.
+- RTL8367D/RB-VC chip ID 0x6642 revision 0x0030 uses CPU7/EXT1.
 
 SDK baseline
 ------------
-  rd05-rgmii-calibrate apply 0 6 0 0 5 1
+  rd05-rgmii-calibrate sdk
 
-Arguments:
-  SOC_TX SOC_RX SW_TX SW_TXC SW_RX SSC
+Expected values:
+  SOC_TX=0 SOC_RX=6 SW_TX=0 SW_TXC=0 SW_RX=5 SSC=1
+
+V38.3 calibration safety
+------------------------
